2327
01:35:28,619 --> 01:35:30,552
-I know our affair wasn't
set up from this film,

2328
01:35:30,586 --> 01:35:33,728
but let's be part ofthe loose ends festival, anyhow.

2329
01:35:33,762 --> 01:35:40,217
♪♪

2330
01:35:40,251 --> 01:35:41,736
-[Imitates monkey]

2331
01:35:41,770 --> 01:35:43,668
♪♪

2332
01:35:43,703 --> 01:35:45,843
-Oh, look, you can see my house.

2333
01:35:45,878 --> 01:35:49,847
♪♪

2334
01:35:49,882 --> 01:35:51,849
-Drive me to the mall.

2335
01:35:51,884 --> 01:35:54,852
♪♪

2336
01:35:54,887 --> 01:35:57,234
-We got a planet
to populate, honey.

2337
01:35:57,268 --> 01:35:59,581
-I'm already bored, Tang.

2338
01:35:59,615 --> 01:36:02,480
♪♪

2339
01:36:02,515 --> 01:36:03,378
-Zzz-z-z-z!

2340
01:36:03,412 --> 01:36:04,689
-Mr. Scott.

2341
01:36:04,724 --> 01:36:06,622
Make an entry in the ship's log.

2342
01:36:06,657 --> 01:36:10,281
-[Speaking gibberish]

2343
01:36:10,316 --> 01:36:11,593
-...is retiring

2344
01:36:11,627 --> 01:36:13,802
from the third planet
of the Solaris system.

2345
01:36:13,837 --> 01:36:16,805
As this planet was here
before unknown...

2346
01:36:16,840 --> 01:36:17,944
-Talking real fast,

2347
01:36:17,979 --> 01:36:19,221
like you know what
you're talking about, yes.

2348
01:36:19,256 --> 01:36:20,567
-From this day forward,

2349
01:36:20,602 --> 01:36:22,155
third planet of Solaris

2350
01:36:22,190 --> 01:36:24,675
will be known
as the blue planet.

2351
01:36:24,709 --> 01:36:27,057
We designate it Planet...

2352
01:36:27,091 --> 01:36:28,058
Earth.

2353
01:36:28,092 --> 01:36:29,404
-Earth?
-Oh, come on.

2354
01:36:29,438 --> 01:36:30,577
Who made you God?

2355
01:36:30,612 --> 01:36:33,477
-Oh, man evolved
from Tang, right.

2356
01:36:33,511 --> 01:36:35,375
We better get out of here.
-That means we better go.

2357
01:36:35,410 --> 01:36:36,376
-That means my great
great-grandmother

2358
01:36:36,411 --> 01:36:37,895
was really, really hot.

2359
01:36:37,930 --> 01:36:39,586
-Was she?
-We got to go figure out a way

2360
01:36:39,621 --> 01:36:41,416
to change ourselves back.
-You have a picture?

2361
01:36:41,450 --> 01:36:43,073
♪♪

2362
01:36:43,107 --> 01:36:44,729
[Doors creak]

2363
01:36:44,764 --> 01:36:47,767
[Doors whir]

2364
01:36:47,802 --> 01:36:49,804
[Doors thud and clank]

2365
01:36:52,461 --> 01:36:54,429
-Hey, you know what?
These, uh --

2366
01:36:54,463 --> 01:36:57,742
Ugh, these Isaac Asimov

2367
01:36:57,777 --> 01:36:59,054
sideburns come off.

2368
01:36:59,089 --> 01:37:00,987
-They're just taped on.
-They're phony.

2369
01:37:01,022 --> 01:37:03,334
-Oh, that's what it means
to be Isaac Asimov, I guess.

2370
01:37:03,369 --> 01:37:05,716
-Yeah, but he probably
already thought of that.

2371
01:37:05,750 --> 01:37:07,822
-Yeah.
Instead of a doomsday machine,

2372
01:37:07,856 --> 01:37:11,066
I guess it kind of turned out
to be a dorks-day machine.

2373
01:37:11,101 --> 01:37:13,586
-Well, it could be worse.
-Oh?

2374
01:37:13,620 --> 01:37:15,139
-Could have been
a Doris Day machine.

2375
01:37:15,174 --> 01:37:16,520
-[Laughs] Oh.

2376
01:37:16,554 --> 01:37:18,246
-Good...
-Come on, you guys.

2377
01:37:18,280 --> 01:37:20,386
It's time to read
some letters here.

2378
01:37:20,420 --> 01:37:21,870
Cambot, let's...

2379
01:37:21,905 --> 01:37:23,009
Oops.
You lost your head.

2380
01:37:23,044 --> 01:37:24,700
-That was my skull.
-Oh, that's too bad.

2381
01:37:24,735 --> 01:37:25,909
That's okay.
-Alright.

2382
01:37:25,943 --> 01:37:29,084
Here we go, Cambot.
Put that up on the screen.

2383
01:37:29,119 --> 01:37:32,329
"MST 3000, I'm writing
a response to you guys,

2384
01:37:32,363 --> 01:37:33,744
and one episode in specific.

2385
01:37:33,778 --> 01:37:36,781
I believe 'Robot Holocaust'
was the name.

2386
01:37:36,816 --> 01:37:38,991
The one in which a man
possessed valuable knowledge,

2387
01:37:39,025 --> 01:37:41,269
and was transformed
into a vegetable-like being

2388
01:37:41,303 --> 01:37:42,995
because of his inability
to cooperate."

2389
01:37:43,029 --> 01:37:44,375
-Avocado Boy.
-Yep.

2390
01:37:44,410 --> 01:37:46,101
-Yeah.
-And we had a contest

2391
01:37:46,136 --> 01:37:49,173
to see who could come upwith a name for the avocado guy,

2392
01:37:49,208 --> 01:37:51,866
and here's his entry.

2393
01:37:51,900 --> 01:37:52,970
He's the winner, by the way.

2394
01:37:53,005 --> 01:37:54,592
Here, he gave us four.

2395
01:37:54,627 --> 01:37:56,077
Skip the Couch Potato.

2396
01:37:56,111 --> 01:37:57,595
Let's have a picture
of that guy, Cambot.

2397
01:37:57,630 --> 01:37:58,493
-You call me.

2398
01:37:58,527 --> 01:38:02,221
-A Man from P.R.O.D.U.C.E.

2399
01:38:02,255 --> 01:38:05,293
A Weeble-O Named Chloro-Phil.

2400
01:38:05,327 --> 01:38:07,812
And The Eighth Wonder
of the Guacamole.

2401
01:38:07,847 --> 01:38:10,850
-[Laughs]
-So, that's from...

2402
01:38:10,885 --> 01:38:13,301
James S. Calstrom, Bloomington.

2403
01:38:13,335 --> 01:38:16,476
-The winner of the brainstorm.
-Yeah, he won the brainstorm.

2404
01:38:16,511 --> 01:38:19,272
Thanks, all who entered
that one, by the way,

2405
01:38:19,307 --> 01:38:22,758
and here's this next one.

2406
01:38:22,793 --> 01:38:24,450
"Dear Sir or 'Bot,

2407
01:38:24,484 --> 01:38:26,659
one lonely, depressing
Saturday night,

2408
01:38:26,693 --> 01:38:28,730
I happened to switch
to Channel 49,

2409
01:38:28,764 --> 01:38:30,697
and found 'MST 3000.'

2410
01:38:30,732 --> 01:38:31,940
It was love at first laugh.

2411
01:38:31,975 --> 01:38:35,081
I was instantly hooked.
Now my life has meaning."

2412
01:38:35,116 --> 01:38:36,496
-That's pretty sad, really.

2413
01:38:36,531 --> 01:38:37,981
-"Anyway, it's a great show.

2414
01:38:38,015 --> 01:38:40,949
I've shown it
to several of my friends,

2415
01:38:40,984 --> 01:38:42,192
and they say they all like it.

2416
01:38:42,226 --> 01:38:44,953
Even my wife likes it,
and she is not an SF fan."

2417
01:38:44,988 --> 01:38:46,092
What's SF mean?

2418
01:38:46,127 --> 01:38:48,750
-Uh, San Francisco.
-Oh, okay.

2419
01:38:48,784 --> 01:38:53,410
-Anyway, the last one here isfrom a father and daughter team.

2420
01:38:53,444 --> 01:38:55,688
-Do they dance, too?
-I don't know.

2421
01:38:55,722 --> 01:38:57,621
"We would like information
about the fan club.

2422
01:38:57,655 --> 01:38:58,898
We would also like to know

2423
01:38:58,933 --> 01:39:02,591
if there's a special club group
for Tom Servo."

2424
01:39:02,626 --> 01:39:03,972
-You betcha.
-Wow.

2425
01:39:04,007 --> 01:39:05,732
"Ever since his head exploded
trying to think

2426
01:39:05,767 --> 01:39:08,149
of something good to say
about 'The Bride Vanishes,'

2427
01:39:08,183 --> 01:39:10,979
we realized he has a rare
and special honesty.

2428
01:39:11,014 --> 01:39:12,981
It's good that you didn't ask
for good comments about

2429
01:39:13,016 --> 01:39:14,155
'Project Moon Base' --

2430
01:39:14,189 --> 01:39:16,122
the consequences
would be unthinkable."

2431
01:39:16,157 --> 01:39:18,090
That's from Ken--
-I shutter at the thought.

2432
01:39:18,124 --> 01:39:21,093
-Yeah, Kenneth J. Plotkin
and Sarah E. Plotkin,

2433
01:39:21,127 --> 01:39:23,681
the Plotkin Family Bellringers.

2434
01:39:23,716 --> 01:39:25,028
Well, that's it.
-The Family Plotkin.

2435
01:39:25,062 --> 01:39:26,305
Tom Servo, you want to give them

2436
01:39:26,339 --> 01:39:27,720
the mailing address?
-Sure.

2437
01:39:27,754 --> 01:39:29,273
-Cambot, put it up
on the screen, there.

2438
01:39:29,308 --> 01:39:31,966
-Love to. It's the
"Mystery Science Theater 3000"

2439
01:39:32,000 --> 01:39:34,106
Information Club.

2440
01:39:34,140 --> 01:39:39,801
PO Box 5325, Hopkins,
Minnesota 55343.

2441
01:39:39,835 --> 01:39:41,389
-Alright, that's the end
of the experiment.

2442
01:39:41,423 --> 01:39:42,838
What do you think, sirs?

2443
01:39:42,873 --> 01:39:45,358
-♪ I think I'll file
this thing for you ♪

2444
01:39:45,393 --> 01:39:48,016
♪ As I always seem to do

2445
01:39:48,051 --> 01:39:49,949
♪ I like working
for you, Clay ♪

2446
01:39:49,984 --> 01:39:52,538
♪ 'Cause you're
a really neat guy ♪

2447
01:39:52,572 --> 01:39:55,713
-Well, I think
you should file this, Larry.

2448
01:39:55,748 --> 01:39:57,577
-'Kay.

2449
01:39:57,612 --> 01:39:58,958
-Ahh.

2450
01:39:58,993 --> 01:40:02,306
Until next time, pasty boy.

2451
01:40:03,998 --> 01:40:13,352
♪♪

2452
01:40:13,386 --> 01:40:22,809
♪♪

2453
01:40:22,844 --> 01:40:32,233
♪♪

2454
01:40:32,267 --> 01:40:41,690
♪♪

2455
01:40:41,725 --> 01:40:51,079
♪♪

2456
01:40:51,114 --> 01:41:00,606
♪♪

2457
01:41:00,640 --> 01:41:10,064
♪♪

